-- A call written with named arguments is read through like a positional one
-- (smucclaw/l4-ide#1033). `named and negated` asks for `big` of n and for n not
-- to be above 3 at once, which only reading the call through can see; base left
-- the named call an opaque atom and reported nothing. `named and narrower` is the
-- control: n above 3 but not above 4 is satisfiable.

GIVEN k IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `big` k IF k > 3

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `named and negated` IF
      (`big` WITH k IS n)
  AND NOT n > 3

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `named and narrower` IF
      (`big` WITH k IS n)
  AND NOT n > 4
